{0 JSON}

{!Workero.JSON} reads and writes JSON values of type [Jsonkit.t]. It does not
re-export jsonkit. Add [jsonkit] to your Dune [libraries] and [jsonkit.ppx]
to [preprocess] when you derive decoders:

{@dune[
(executable
 (name main)
 (modes wasm)
 (preprocess
  (pps jsonkit.ppx))
 (libraries workero jsonkit))
]}

This handler decodes the request body into a record and returns JSON. The
handler chooses the response for a decode error:

{@ocaml[
open Jsonkit.Primitives

type user = { name : string; age : int } [@@deriving json]

let handler req _env _ctx =
  match Workero.JSON.decode user_of_json req with
  | Ok user -> Workero.JSON.response (user_to_json user)
  | Error message -> Workero.JSON.error message

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

{!Workero.JSON.decode} reads the body once and returns [Error message] for
invalid JSON or when the decoder raises [Jsonkit.Of_json_error]. It does not
send a 400 response. Other decoder exceptions escape unless you catch them.
{!Workero.JSON.parse} reads a [Jsonkit.t] without decoding it and also returns
a result. {!Workero.JSON.request} instead raises [Jsonkit.Of_string_error] on
invalid JSON; an uncaught exception makes the runtime answer with status 500.

{!Workero.JSON.response} sends compact JSON with status 200 and
[content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8] by default.
{!Workero.JSON.error} sends an [{"error": message}] object with status 400 by
default. You can select another status for either response.

For a binding that gives you a JavaScript value, {!Workero.JSON.of_js}
converts its JSON representation to [Jsonkit.t]. It follows
[JSON.stringify]: it drops object fields with [undefined] or function values
and raises [Invalid_argument] for values with no JSON representation, such as
a cyclic object or a [BigInt]. {!Workero.JSON.to_js} converts [Jsonkit.t] to a
new JavaScript value; it raises [Invalid_argument] for [nan] or an infinite
float. See {!Workero.JSON} for these functions' complete contracts.

Without the ppx, write a decoder that matches on [`Assoc] and uses the
[Jsonkit.Of_json] functions for each field. Raise [Jsonkit.Of_json_error] for
a missing field. {!Workero.JSON.decode} turns it into [Error]. See
{!Workero.JSON} for an example. See
{{!page-requests}Requests and responses} for other body formats.
